  "usage_note": "Spelling varies from word to word. Many common **co-** words are written as one word, especially in American English (*coworker*, *cofounder*), and some are also written with a hyphen (*co-worker*); a hyphen is usual before **o** (*co-owner*). **Cooperate** and **coordinate** are usually one word in American English.",
